  "notes": "West leads the ♠Q which South wins. South has 8 top tricks (2 in spades, 4 in hearts, and 2 in clubs). South has finessing positions in both diamonds and clubs.\n\nIt is important that South takes the diamond finesse before the club finesse. If South takes the club finesse first and it loses, East will clear the spades. If West has 5 or more spades, South will no longer be able to take advantage of the ♦A being onside. West will take his ♦A and cash out the spades.\n\nIf South leads a diamond to the ♦K at trick 2 and that finesse loses, South will still be able to make his contract when West has the ♣Q. East will clear spades, but South can take 9 tricks, via the club finesse, without losing the lead.",
  "commentary_paragraphs": [
